- runtime/somart/codec.py      NumPy port of motionbricks/model/soma/kernels.py and
                               motionbricks/model/kernels.py (encode, decode, conditions,
                               endpoint correction); site/js/codec.js ports the same to JavaScript
- runtime/somart/skeleton.py   BVH loading logic ported from motionbricks/io/bvh.py
- runtime/somart/contract.py   constants from motionbricks/model/contract.py and soma_n1.json

The upstream ONNX exporter (tools/onnx) is used unmodified from third_party/ (not redistributed).
Changes relative to upstream: vectorised NumPy implementation, batching, and the additional
velocity-matching and contact-aware options in codec.py.

Model weights: NVIDIA Open Model Agreement ("Licensed by NVIDIA Corporation under the NVIDIA Open
Model License"). site/models/ holds an INT8-quantized derivative for the web demo, stored in a split GGUF file
whose INT8 matrix weights are re-coded with ggml Q5_0 blocks (tools/gguf/build_gguf.py).
site/data/bank.* holds output of that model.

SOMA body mesh (site/data/soma_mesh.*) and rig (site/data/skeleton.json): extracted from the upstream
MotionBricks asset soma_base_skel_minimal_no_root.usd (tools/extract_mesh.py), NVIDIA, CC BY 4.0.

Motion capture (site/data/windows.*, clips.*, styles/*; targets for the network, not played back):
- 100STYLE dataset by Ian Mason, Sebastian Starke and Taku Komura, "Real-Time Style Modelling of Human
  Locomotion via Feature-Wise Transformations and Local Motion Phases" (2022),
  https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.8127870, licensed CC BY 4.0 (https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/).
  Clips named 100STYLE/*.
- CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database. The data used in this project was obtained from mocap.cs.cmu.edu.
  The database was created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217. Free for all uses (it may be copied, modified or
  redistributed; it may not be resold directly). Clips named CMU/<subject>_<trial>.
Both modified: retargeted onto the SOMA rig (arms re-solved with two-bone IK), trimmed, resampled to 30 fps and
quantized (tools/mocap/style100.py, tools/mocap/cmu.py, tools/export_web_data.py). The joint limits
(configs/skeletons/soma_joint_limits.json, site/data/joint_limits.json) are fitted on the same clips, the
hinge axes (configs/skeletons/soma_hinges.json) on the model's own output, and the relaxed hand pose is authored.

site/vendor/ redistributes, unmodified: onnxruntime-web 1.31.1 (Microsoft, MIT), three.js 0.170.0 (MIT);
site/coi-serviceworker.js (Guido Zuidhof, MIT). Licence texts are in site/vendor/.
